Finding: {"title":"handleDisputeCreated contains dead code (always-null piPaymentMethod branch) and an unnecessary dynamic import of an already-imported module","severity":"LOW","area":"Stripe webhook — dead code","files":["src/app/api/stripe-webhook/route.ts"],"detail":"Lines 908-942: piPaymentMethod is computed via a ternary that is provably always null (`typeof dispute.payment_intent === 'object' && dispute.payment_intent ? null : null`), then immediately voided with `void piPaymentMethod` to suppress the unused-var lint. The actual PM-blocking logic instead re-fetches the charge via a dynamic `import('@/lib/stripe')` even though stripeClient is already imported at module scope.","impact":"No functional bug — the real block logic works via the charge lookup — but the dead ternary and duplicate/dynamic import are a maintenance trap; a future editor could assume piPaymentMethod does something.","recommendation":"Delete piPaymentMethod and the void line entirely; replace the dynamic `await import('@/lib/stripe')` with the module-level stripeClient import.","confidence":"high"}
